      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Right atrial monophasic action potential was recorded using a suction electrode catheter in 20 patients with chronic cor pulmonale. The duration of right atrial monophasic action potential was recorded using suction electrode catheter in 20 patients with chronic corpulmonale. The duration of right atrial monophasic action potential was 397 +/- 17 msec, longer than the normal value of 325 +/- 37 msec found in 30 normal subjects. The conclusion of our work is that the long right atrial monophasic action potential duration may explain the sinus rhythm stability and the rarity of atrial arrhythmias in chronic cor pulmonale."},
